"distance":0.3072,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"IND","distance":0.322,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Titans are 1-8 through week 10 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 239 to 167. Neither side has held up so far, with the offense 26th in EPA per play and the defense 29th in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the highest no-huddle rate and the 3rd fewest defenders in the box in the league.","offense":"The Titans offense has struggled, ranking 25th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the highest no-huddle rate and the 2nd highest RPO rate in the league. Cam Ward has run the passing game, with Wan'Dale Robinson leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Titans have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 29th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Their one bright spot has been takeaways per game, where they rank 10th. Jeffery Simmons has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Jacob Martin, who has 7.5 sacks while playing only 59% of the snaps, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Schematically, they have the 3rd fewest defenders in the box in the league.","special":"The Titans have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 94% of field goals, which is one of the best in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the defensive line, about 25% of the money on the books. Their linebackers were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Cam Ward has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,714 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Wan'Dale Robinson and Carnell Tate leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. Tony Pollard has handled most of the work in the backfield with 80% of the carries. On defense, Jacob Martin leads the team with 7.5 sacks and Amani Hooker has picked off 5 passes.","coaching":"Brian Daboll is calling the offense and Robert Saleh is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2024 Commanders under Kliff Kingsbury and the 2023 Colts under Shane Steichen. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Seahawks under Mike Macdonald and the 2023 Bears.","trends":"The offense went from 30th in EPA per play in 2025 to 26th so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 28th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 29th so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 0% to 18%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}